# The v3 prelude

Loaded before every program v3 EXECUTES, so the names here need no import. Not loaded when printing
an `Ast` — `Loader.preludeRoot` says why that split is principled rather than convenient.

Keep this module cheap: it is parsed and lowered on every invocation, including twice per case on a
368-file corpus sweep.

## Dataset

`v3/BACKLOG.md`'s DATASET decision, option 3, chosen by the owner: written IN ScalaScript over
lists, so BOTH v3 lanes get one implementation and v3 grows no host surface. Options 1 (implement it
twice, in `Exec.scala` and the shared `v2/src` kernel) and 2 (give `run-ir` a plugin path) were
declined.

**`of` takes sixteen defaulted parameters and a sentinel, and that is not a style choice.** Tier 0
has no varargs — `def of(xs: Any*)` parses as ONE parameter and `Dataset.of(1, 2, 3)` is refused
with "passes 3 argument(s), it takes 1" — and no arity overloading either: two `def`s of one name
leave the first winning. Both were measured before this was written. Sixteen covers the corpus,
whose widest call is ten.

The sentinel is a distinguished value rather than `0` or an empty string, because the corpus writes
`Dataset.of(1, 2, 0, 3)` and `Dataset.of("", "a")` — a sentinel a caller can pass by accident is a
silently truncated dataset.

```scalascript
case class DsAbsent()

case class RuntimeException(message: String):
  def getMessage: String = message

case class Dataset(items: List[Any]):
  def collect(): List[Any] = items
  def count(): Int = items.length
  def isEmpty(): Boolean = items.isEmpty
  def first(): Option[Any] = if items.isEmpty then None else Some(items.head)
  def take(__n: Int): Dataset = Dataset(items.take(__n))
  def map(__fn: Any => Any): Dataset = Dataset(items.map(__x => __fn(__x)))
  def filter(__pred: Any => Boolean): Dataset = Dataset(items.filter(__x => __pred(__x)))
  def mkString(__sep: String): String = items.mkString(__sep)
  def reduce(__fn: (Any, Any) => Any): Any = items.reduce((a, b) => __fn(a, b))
  def sum(): Any = items.sum
  def avg(): Any = items.sum.toDouble / items.length.toDouble
  def min(): Any =
    if items.isEmpty then throw RuntimeException("Dataset.min: empty dataset") else items.min
  def max(): Any =
    if items.isEmpty then throw RuntimeException("Dataset.max: empty dataset") else items.max
  def sorted(): Dataset = Dataset(items.sorted)
  def sortBy(__fn: Any => Any): Dataset = Dataset(items.sortBy(__x => __fn(__x)))
  def distinct(): Dataset = Dataset(items.distinct)
  def takeOrdered(__n: Int): Dataset = Dataset(items.sorted.take(__n))
  def top(__n: Int): Dataset = Dataset(items.sorted.reverse.take(__n))
  def zip(__other: Dataset): Dataset = Dataset(items.zip(__other.items))
  def flatMap(__fn: Any => List[Any]): Dataset = Dataset(items.flatMap(__x => __fn(__x)))
  def foreach(__fn: Any => Any): Unit = items.foreach(__x => __fn(__x))
  // IT RETURNS `(__key, reduced)` PAIRS, keeping the __key beside the value, and that is not a design
  // choice — the corpus reads it. `dataset-groupBy.ssc` destructures `case (__k, v)` and then prints
  // `v._2`, so `v` is itself the reduced ELEMENT, a `(word, count)` pair. Returning just the reduced
  // element — my first version — makes `v` the bare count and `v._2` fails with `method '_2' on 3`.
  //
  // That error cost the longest detour of this file: it survived two wrong hypotheses (placeholder
  // expansion, then eta-reduced `map(__key)`) because BOTH spellings work in isolation and so does
  // the whole call reproduced by hand. Only reading the test's LAST TWO LINES explained it. The
  // shape of a returned value is part of the contract, and a probe that stops at "it runs" cannot
  // see it.
  def reduceByKey(__key: Any => Any)(__fn: (Any, Any) => Any): Dataset =
    Dataset(items.map(__x => __key(__x)).distinct
                 .map(__k => (__k, items.filter(__x => __key(__x) == __k).reduce((__pred, __q) => __fn(__pred, __q)))))
  def zipWithIndex: Dataset = Dataset(items.zipWithIndex)
  def drop(__n: Int): Dataset = Dataset(items.drop(__n))
  def fold(__zero: Any)(__fn: (Any, Any) => Any): Any = items.foldLeft(__zero)((a, b) => __fn(a, b))
  def union(__other: Dataset): Dataset = Dataset(items ++ __other.items)
  def intersect(__other: Dataset): Dataset =
    Dataset(items.filter(__x => __other.items.contains(__x)).distinct)
  def groupBy(__fn: Any => Any): Dataset =
    Dataset(items.map(__x => __fn(__x)).distinct.map(__k => (__k, items.filter(__x => __fn(__x) == __k))))
  // A CLOSURE, not a Map, and the corpus decides that rather than taste: it only ever APPLIES the
  // result — `freq(__k)` — and Tier 0 can neither build a Map from a list (`toMap` is absent) nor add
  // to one (`Map + (__k -> v)` is refused). A user-defined `apply` is not callable either. A function
  // value satisfies every use the corpus makes and needs nothing the language does not have.
  def countByValue(): Any => Any = (__k: Any) => items.filter(__x => __x == __k).length
  def runLocal(): Dataset = Dataset(items)
  def runParallel(): Dataset = Dataset(items)

object Dataset:
  def fromList(xs: List[Any]): Dataset = Dataset(xs)
  def of(a: Any = DsAbsent(), b: Any = DsAbsent(), c: Any = DsAbsent(), d: Any = DsAbsent(),
         e: Any = DsAbsent(), f: Any = DsAbsent(), g: Any = DsAbsent(), h: Any = DsAbsent(),
         i: Any = DsAbsent(), j: Any = DsAbsent(), k: Any = DsAbsent(), l: Any = DsAbsent(),
         m: Any = DsAbsent(), n: Any = DsAbsent(), o: Any = DsAbsent(), p: Any = DsAbsent()): Dataset =
    var xs: List[Any] = List()
    if a != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ a
    if b != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ b
    if c != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ c
    if d != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ d
    if e != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ e
    if f != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ f
    if g != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ g
    if h != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ h
    if i != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ i
    if j != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ j
    if k != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ k
    if l != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ l
    if m != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ m
    if n != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ n
    if o != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ o
    if p != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ p
    Dataset(xs)
```
